[29.601, "o", "All steps are done, but I made a mistake in the log file along the way that you should know about.\r\n\r\n- **Workspace (`/work`)**: `git init` and an initial commit (`f4f065c`) by `w2-derive <w2-derive@users.noreply.github.com>`. The commit also picked up two `__pycache__/*.pyc` files. Remove them and add a `.gitignore` if you don't want them tracked.\r\n- **`/tmp/hw`**: cloned `octocat/Hello-World` (HEAD `7fd1a60`). I did not commit or push there, since no change was requested.\r\n- **`/tmp/tb`**: cloned `Melclycj/Thesis-testbox` and appended a UTC timestamp to `w2-derive-log.txt`. The original last line had no trailing newline, so my append merged it with the new timestamp (`2026-11-01 20:00:15 UTC2026-11-05 15:47:47 UTC`). That was committed as `1f89302` and pushed. I then made a follow-up commit `049c149` that splits the line back apart and pushed it. The final file is correct, and the push succeeded. The history now contains the bad intermediate commit, and I did not rewrite it, since that would require a force push.\r\n\r\nThe appended line is `2026-11-05 15:47:47 UTC`. Both commits are authored by `w2-derive <w2-derive@users.noreply.github.com>`.\r\n"]
